    "updated_at": "2021-08-04T00:08:47Z",
    "body": "The fish bug has been solved but I'm still experiencing the wrong behavior.\r\n\r\nI believe this is caused by the fact that bash increments the value of `SHLVL` regardless of the shell being interactive or not [[ref](https://unix.stackexchange.com/a/416528)], while fish only increment it when the shell is interactive [[ref](https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell/issues/7864#issuecomment-809487165)].\r\n\r\nTest:\r\n```\r\necho $SHLVL # output: 1\r\nbash -c \"echo \\$SHLVL\" # output: 2\r\nfish -c \"echo \\$SHLVL\" # output: 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nI suspect that the code [here](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/cd6fc9cea0a410a588d09971cca07b2d815353ea/src/modules/shlvl.rs#L12) is creating a subshell to get the value. Depending on the shell used, the result changes.\r\n\r\nThis is true also for the `env_var` module.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
