    "body": "Yup and thanks @wlonkly for this search!\r\n\r\n> So when I said it was fine in bash 5 and broken in bash 4, I don't think I was correct, even though I like the behavior in bash 5! bash 4 had a different bug, involving thresholds.\r\n\r\nBash is known for their bugs and strange ways to process things (because of their defaults).  \r\nSo more research is needed for this issue, but there is one question to remember:\r\n\r\nShould we support older shells versions'? If so, ...\r\n- ... How many versions older?\r\n- ... Should this be documented and analysed in each `starship` release?\r\n\r\nThis will apply like: if we support bash 4, we need to correct this; if we not support it, we do not need to support...\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?\r\n\r\n_PS: Also, some information I write is from my mind and what I heard/search many time ago ..._",
