    "updated_at": "2023-02-16T20:35:59Z",
    "body": "I think this might be easy to fix: add a `--shlvl` option to `starship prompt` like the `--jobs` option works now. If set, use it; if not set, fall back to the environment variable. Then we're guaranteed to have the SHLVL of the current shell, regardless of how a shell happens to invoke `starship prompt`, and thus regardless of bash version. \r\n\r\n(I'm not even sure the fallback is required, if it's safe to assume that anyone upgrading starship also upgrades their starship init shell script.) ",
